      },
      "message": "feat(deburr): a policy for edges out of the cone's reach\n\n3D Deburr gets the setting `unreachable` (finishing3d::UnreachableEdges):\n`SkipWithNote` (the default) leaves an edge that climbs steeper than the\ncone's flank and names the count in a note, as each earlier Deburr did.\n`Refuse` refuses the operation by name before a path is built.\n\nThe policy is a field of DeburrParams and OpParams::Deburr. The project\nfile reads an absent key as skip_with_note (serde default, no version\nstep). The digest writes one byte for Refuse only. The Deburr page has\nthe combo \"Unreachable edges\"; MCP takes the field in a params patch.\n\nPinned by crates/motion/tests/deburr_unreachable.rs and\ncrates/app/tests/deburr_unreachable.rs.\n\nFixes #1889\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
